<Project>
  <!--
    Centralize Microsoft.Azure.Cosmos on a single version across every project
    under src/.

    The repo was mid-migration: a few engines (BenefitEngine, FeeScheduleEngine,
    NcciEngine) were bumped to 3.62.1 while most services, the shared
    Infrastructure library, and the remaining engines stayed on 3.62.0. Any
    service whose reference closure spans both versions collected two copies of
    the Cosmos native runtime assets, which fails `dotnet publish` with
    NETSDK1152 ("multiple publish output files with the same relative path") and
    trips NU1605 package-downgrade errors at restore.

    This override lives in a .targets file (imported after each project's own
    PackageReference items) so the Update reliably overrides the per-project
    version metadata, unifying the whole graph on one version without editing
    every csproj. Bump this single value for future Cosmos upgrades.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Update="Microsoft.Azure.Cosmos" Version="3.62.1" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
